{#
    Small full-page loading overlay shown the moment the customer submits the
    checkout "complete" step, for as long as Topi is the payment method they picked.

    Hooked into `sylius_shop.checkout.complete.content.form` (receives `order` as
    context, see @SyliusShop/checkout/complete/content/form.html.twig), sibling to
    the `navigation` entry rendering the "Place order" button in that same hook.

    Why this is needed: unlike the "Buy now" buttons (checkout_button_*.html.twig),
    which redirect via a JS `fetch()` call, the regular checkout's "Place order"
    button is a plain form submit — Sylius completes the order server-side, then
    CaptureAction (src/Payum/CaptureAction.php) calls Topi's API to create an offer
    and throws a Payum HttpRedirect to the hosted checkout, all before the browser
    sees a response. That round trip has no built-in visual feedback, so a slow
    network/Topi response can look like a stuck page. This overlay is shown
    synchronously on the form's `submit` event — before the browser navigates away —
    and simply stays on screen (nothing hides it again) until either the redirect to
    Topi lands or a fresh page load replaces it (e.g. on a validation error, which
    reloads the page and never runs this script again until it re-renders).
#}
{% set order = hookable_metadata.context.order %}
{# Collection::last() returns `false` (not null) on an empty collection — see
   @SyliusShop/order/thank_you/content/payment_instruction.html.twig for the same
   guard against that. #}
{% set lastPayment = order is not null ? order.payments.last() : false %}
{% set gatewayConfig = lastPayment != false and lastPayment.method is not null ? lastPayment.method.gatewayConfig : null %}
{% if gatewayConfig is not null and gatewayConfig.factoryName == 'topi_payment' %}
    <div
        id="topi-checkout-redirect-overlay"
        hidden
        class="position-fixed top-0 start-0 w-100 h-100 d-flex flex-column align-items-center justify-content-center gap-3"
        style="z-index: 1080; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);"
    >
        <div class="spinner-border" role="status" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <p class="mb-0">{{ 'eiling_io_sylius_topi.checkout.redirecting'|trans }}</p>
    </div>
    <script>
        (function () {
            var overlay = document.getElementById('topi-checkout-redirect-overlay');
            var form = document.querySelector('form[action="{{ path('sylius_shop_checkout_complete') }}"]');
            if (!overlay || !form) {
                return;
            }

            // `submit` only fires once the browser's own (HTML5) validation has
            // passed — form.html.twig sets `novalidate`, so Sylius' own server-side
            // validation is what actually gates a valid order; on a validation
            // error the whole page reloads and this listener is simply gone again,
            // so the overlay can never get stuck open in front of an error message.
            form.addEventListener('submit', function () {
                overlay.hidden = false;

                var submitButton = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');
                if (submitButton) {
                    submitButton.disabled = true;
                }
            });
        })();
    </script>
{% endif %}
